From 94596d413d5c94ec1f6b5a23bad7b4ff2c909c04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <miroslav.mraz@techmania.cz>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:32:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH v1 08/22] arm64: dts: qcom: sc7180: add GPI DMA engines and
 wire up QUP

Add the two GPI DMA controllers present in the QUPv3 wrappers and wire
their tx/rx channels to every geni I2C and SPI SE. Without them the geni
drivers fall back to FIFO mode after logging "Failed to get tx DMA ch"
for each SE at boot.

The controllers use the qcom,sm6350-gpi-dma programming model (SC7180 and
SM6350/SM7125 share the same GPI hardware); the register windows, IRQs,
channel masks and SMMU stream IDs match the wrapper layout.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7180.dtsi | 101 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 101 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7180.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc7180.dtsi
index 70fbfb31d4a4..51e637559447 100644
